{"nodes": [{"id": "qa_md", "label": "Tribunal Q&A Preparation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "qa_lazy_sweep_on_read", "label": "Lazy Sweep-on-Read Pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Auto-completion runs lazily inside the same transaction as the read that follows, instead of a cron job, so it needs no scheduler, stays transactionally consistent with what the user is about to see, costs nothing for inactive families, and is concurrency-safe via FOR UPDATE row locks; trade-off is payouts wait until someone opens the app."}, {"id": "qa_for_update_locking_pattern", "label": "SELECT ... FOR UPDATE Locking Pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Row-level lock taken inside a single transaction (validate, complete, offerBounty, runAutoCompleteSweep) so a concurrent second request blocks, then re-evaluates the committed status and is rejected cleanly, making double-minting of coins impossible without load-tested infrastructure."}, {"id": "qa_two_service_worker_architecture", "label": "Two Service Worker Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Workbox SW (offline caching, autoUpdate) and firebase-messaging-sw.js (background push, own scope) coexist without conflict because Firebase registers its worker at a distinct push scope."}, {"id": "qa_firebase_sw_vite_plugin", "label": "generate-firebase-sw Vite Plugin", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A service worker must be served as a static file at a fixed URL so it cannot go through Vite's bundler and read import.meta.env; a custom buildStart hook writes public/firebase-messaging-sw.js with config baked in from the same env vars the app uses, avoiding config drift or a runtime fetch race on a cold-woken worker."}, {"id": "qa_firebase_auth_verification_chain", "label": "Firebase Auth Verification Chain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Firebase answers who the user is (stateless local JWT verification against cached Google public keys); the backend's own family_members RBAC answers what they may do, decoupled from Firebase UID via upsertUserFromAuth."}, {"id": "qa_layered_architecture", "label": "Middleware / Routes / Services Layering", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Middleware answers 'may this proceed', routes translate HTTP to domain calls with no logic of their own, services hold pure business rules against a transaction client with no HTTP knowledge \u2014 this boundary is what makes 44+ backend unit tests possible with a mock DB client."}, {"id": "qa_sql_injection_defense", "label": "Parameterized Query Defense", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every client.query() call passes user values as $N params, never string-concatenated; the one dynamic SQL fragment (prefClause in notify.js) is guarded by a hardcoded whitelist Set, closing the only apparent injection surface."}, {"id": "qa_test_pyramid", "label": "Deliberate Test Pyramid", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Risk-based unit testing on money-moving/consensus paths plus offline E2E against the Firebase emulator, including a two-browser cross-user validation test; known gaps are the auto-complete sweep, coverage measurement, and push delivery."}, {"id": "qa_two_users_e2e_test", "label": "two-users.spec.js Cross-User E2E Test", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "qa_frontend_layering", "label": "Frontend Extraction Motives (Reuse vs Testability)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Design-system primitives (VButton, VCard, VInput, VSelect, KpiCard) are extracted for reuse across many views; composables and view sub-components with a single consumer (useTimeline, TaskLibrary) are extracted purely for isolation and unit-testability, not reuse."}], "edges": [{"source": "qa_md", "target": "docs_backend_md", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "qa_md", "target": "docs_automatic_testing_e2e_md", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "qa_md", "target": "docs_admin_family_management_plan_md", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "qa_md", "target": "qa_for_update_locking_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "QA.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "qa_for_update_locking_pattern", "target": "docs_backend_activityservice",